.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt IWM 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm iwm
.Nd Intel(R) Dual Band Wireless-AC 8260 and 8265 Driver
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver is a GLDv3-based
.Em 802.11a/b/g/n
wireless NIC driver for the Intel Dual Band Wireless-AC 8260 and 8265
(8000 series) adapters.
It is a port of the OpenBSD
.Nm
driver.
.Pp
It supports station mode in infrastructure networks, open, WEP and
WPA/WPA2 networks (pairwise CCMP keys in hardware, other ciphers in
software), the 2.4 GHz and, where the adapter allows it, 5 GHz bands,
20 and 40 MHz channels, one or two spatial streams with short guard
interval, receive and transmit A-MPDU aggregation, MiRA rate adaptation
for 802.11n and AMRR for legacy rates, firmware location-aware
regulatory support, and suspend and resume.
The driver restarts the device automatically after a firmware error, a
hardware error, a transmit timeout or a change of the RF-kill switch.
.Pp
802.11ac (VHT) rates, background scanning, monitor mode, access point
and IBSS modes, and power save are not supported.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The driver is configured with
.Xr dladm 8 .
It has no
.Pa driver.conf
properties.
The firmware image must be installed in
.Pa /kernel/firmware/iwm
before the driver attaches.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -compact -width Pa
.It Pa /dev/iwm*
Special character device.
.It Pa /kernel/drv/amd64/iwm
64-bit ELF kernel module (x86).
.It Pa /kernel/firmware/iwm/iwm-8000C-36
Firmware for the 8260.
.It Pa /kernel/firmware/iwm/iwm-8265-36
Firmware for the 8265.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dladm 8 ,
.Xr wificonfig 8
